{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"How Swami translates the four kinds of Origami patch into SwiftUI’s state graph.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Reference"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/OrigamiMappings","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI are both reactive dataflow, so the translator"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"targets SwiftUI’s "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"state graph","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — computed properties, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":" —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not imperative functions. Each row below is a rule the codegen applies; the helper"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag"},{"type":"text","text":", …) fills the gaps where a patch has no direct"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"The four rules","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"The-four-rules"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Origami","type":"text"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"SwiftUI","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Pure value patch (Add, Transition\/interpolate, logic)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlin