.animation`","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Animation-%E2%86%92-withAnimation--animation"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Classic Animation"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Pop Animation"},{"text":", and other animation patches drive a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"toward a target over time. In SwiftUI, that’s a state change wrapped in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"text":" or an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animation(_:value:)"},{"text":" modifier on the animated property.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Continuous-time springs that don’t have a stock SwiftUI equivalent get flagged","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by the parser — Swami won’t fake them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Flag, don’t fake","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Flag-dont-fake"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Some Origami semantics don’t have a SwiftUI equivalent. When the parser hits one,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it emits a marker in the IR and codegen surfaces the gap rather than papering over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it. The current list: continuous-time springs, custom JavaScript patches,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"absolute-position layout."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swami\/origamimappings"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"title":"Origami → SwiftUI mappings","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swami"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"]]},"references":{"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Drag":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"tex